From 7cf43f0326f3f7ad8c23f275b26508339b57f52d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:35:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] primitives: precompute m_serialize_size and
 PrecomputedTransactionData on CTransaction

A transaction's sighash midstate (hashPrevouts, hashSequence,
hashOutputs) was recomputed each time a PrecomputedTransactionData was
built for it: in mempool acceptance and again in ConnectBlock for the
same CTransactionRef. GetTotalSize() and GetSerializeSize() also
re-walked the transaction on every call.

Compute both once in CTransaction's constructors and store them in
const members, so they are immutable and safe to share across threads
without atomics:

- m_serialize_size: Serialize() with a SizeComputer seeks by it
  directly, and GetTotalSize() returns it.
- m_precomputed: exposed as GetPrecomputedData().
  PrecomputedTransactionData(const CTransaction &) now copies it;
  CMutableTransaction still hashes, through the new
  PrecomputedTransactionData::Compute().

ConnectBlock and CheckInputsFromMempoolAndCache bind the cached data by
const reference, and MemPoolAccept no longer keeps its own copy in the
workspace.

Trade-off: every constructed CTransaction now pays the three midstate
hashes up front, including transactions that are never script-checked
(e.g. blocks deserialized only to be served or indexed), and
sizeof(CTransaction) grows from 88 to 192 bytes on LP64. Mempool memory
accounting includes the larger object.

Test: cached size and midstate match fresh computation for null and
varied transactions, constructed by copy and by move.
